 "_purpose": "Committed evidence for Phase 19E D128 (qr-19-single-slot-writer-slot-key): the same-machine, same-Vite-tree before/after of the single-slot elision cache under Option A (four independent slots per element). Both sides: scripts/perf_tour.mjs headless swiftshader (the default mode, NOT PERF_GPU=1), PERF_VIEWPORT=both, two runs each; before = the merge tip 2ebe95e731 unmodified, after = the same tree with d128-option-a-prototype.patch applied to src/ui/painter_host.ts (reverted from a disk copy afterwards; the prototype never landed). hudHotDomWrites is compared as a PER-STEP SERIES (the perStep rows), because in this mode the tour renders 39 to 100 frames against the headed golden's 1,400 plus and the count is still climbing through the look step, so it never reaches the steady state where the metric is the run-length-independent anchor tests/hud_perf_budget.baseline.md defines: through the first four steps the eight series agree exactly except where a run rendered markedly fewer frames at that step; at the look and final steps they vary run to run on both sides independent of the shape (the one desktop pair at equal frames reads identical, mobile's after runs sit 7 to 10 writes above its before runs at comparable frames), and since the four-slot cache can only remove writes, an after figure above a before figure is tour variation. The tour corroborates the deductive proof of zero and bounds a hidden hot per-frame cross-kind site to none inside a 27-write spread; it is not itself the proof. THESE ARTIFACTS MUST NEVER BE FED TO ARM 3 (three of the four desktop captures sit at or above the committed anchor 1062, before-run2 on unmodified code, and all are below the tourMinFrames floor) and must not be reused for any GPU-preparation claim (prewarm completed 23 of 33 manifest entries on desktop with the budget nearly exhausted and 3 of 33 on mobile; KHR_parallel_shader_compile is unsupported under swiftshader). The full tour JSONs these rows are extracted from are session artifacts (about 3 MB each), not committed. Every run exited 1 on pre-existing console lines (character asset not preloaded: two on desktop, one on mobile), with zero budget or FCT-burst failures.",
